WEBVTT

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.450
Oh, to sail the bounding bane, to ride the ocean crest.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.680
To scuttle a scupper and muzzle your supper when the sun is in the west.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.180
Oh, to be a jolly tar, to brave the briny dip.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.790
With swabbing and scrubbing and fainting and rubbing.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.170
And a trip on a pip of a ship.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.780
And a trip on a pip of a ship.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.480
And a trip on a pip of a ship.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.460
And a trip on a pip of a sheep.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.630
I don't know what everybody's so happy about.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:09.300
A year and a half of this guff, and a year and a half more to go.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.520
What wouldn't I give to be a civilian?

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.400
and make some real dough.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:26.830
Oh, Zeeb.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.060
What can you do with 90 lousy bucks?

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:34.580
Hey, who said that?

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:35.680
Me.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:37.820
Who are you?

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.640
A friend, Mac, a friend.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:46.250
As we were saying, you ain't exactly happy in the Navy, right?

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:47.570
Right.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.480
So, what's the best thing to do with 90 lousy bucks?

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.460
Get drunk.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:54.780
Right.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.510
See you on the beach.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.620
How do you like the Navy, bud?

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:36.780
It stinks.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.820
Listen, you see those ships out there?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.570
You think they've got engines.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.540
Ha! When they get out to sea...

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:55.750
Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho! Heave ho!

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.930
Oh, yeah. Civilian life.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.980
is better any day.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.190
You said it.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.800
Be your own boss.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.540
Nobody shoves you around.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.820
Your own house,

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.230
in front of your privacy.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.610
Oh, yeah.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:19.560
You ought to see a little place I got in the country.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.240
Flows and birds.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.220
Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.280
A little place I got picked out.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.520
In the country.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:29.960
Flows.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.380
Champa, champi

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:35.880
It's a baby.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:57.520
God.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.890
This is Joan speaking.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:01.020
Oh

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.870
Your boss, McGinty!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.430
Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:12.210
Sorry to bother you, Mackenzie, but are you planning to come to work today?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:13.620
Die.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:14.710
Too hot.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:17.770
Just take the rest of it.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:18.320
they are.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.150
Send your week's salary over right away.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:21.770
Ha!

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:31.850
Here.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:32.910
Take care of the rest.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:33.520
Amen.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.340
All right.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.550
You

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.290
What a dream.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:03.760
You liked it, huh?

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.900
Tell Rick, I gotta be a civilian.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:09.580
It's a cinch.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:10.880
Sign here.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.320
What's this?

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.180
Your discharge.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.060
I fixed it for you.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:19.300
Hey, what's your angle, Mac?

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.050
You'll find out.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.810
Day, money, food, freedom.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.210
Close your eyes.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:30.520
Hey!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.390
What's happened?

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:32.600
Where are the women?

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.230
That was a dream.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:39.930
Now you're gonna see what civilian life is really like.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:42.440
Tire at the age of forty-five, annuity convertible with double indemnity, security for your old age, every man owes it to his son.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:43.120
Yes, I understand.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:49.550
Yes, yes, and there's endowments too, automatic conversion premiums, don't hesitate, do it now.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:50.390
But I...

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.050
Any questions?

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:53.230
Yes, good, good, good, good.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:59.970
Sign here, that will be $134.23 please, that's your first monthly.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.340
Hey, I can retire for free in the Navy.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.940
Ah, yes, but you're not in the Navy.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:07.320
Good day.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:56.730
Civilian life, talk this thing over.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.960
If things are so tough on the outside, why do I...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.900
Don't you go back. It's a cinch. You can re-enlist at your old rate within 90 days.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.660
That's right.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:27.450
What are you doing around here? Cram out of here before I...

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:28.650
Just a minute. Just a minute.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:35.020
It might interest you to know, mate, that I am employed by the United States Navy.
